# Jam readiness: inputs for the builder's decision

9 October 2026, Eastern time. Planner recommendation under existing request `b4ef9b7adaabcd7f7a89582146c2bcbe7bfe4f81`; this is not the builder's readiness judgment or a release claim.

Current inspected Jam source is `990dcbf3ffd15d44c9fccdd88c671866dd5e7218`. It already contains a symbolic, procedural demo. Its package has no Artroom dependency and uses Node's test runner. The original C and E-flat phrase arrays and an application-owned rhythm are described in `notes/2026-10-09-original-demo-source.md`. That note reports 43 cheap source checks, with waveform cases excluded, and a 40-second default clip plan. It explicitly leaves actual browser, listening, audio, native Artroom attachment and release acceptance open. No tests or audio were run for this assessment.

The README's unqualified “Not built yet” is stale. The older Artroom Jam design note labels its platform status against dated Oct 6 sources; those historical limits must not silently become today's development-start gate.

Jam's repository instructions are still binding: depend on published Artroom packages and a deployed room URL; do not import or workspace-link Artroom source. A platform gap becomes a tracked request in Artroom. Until Artroom can host its work, Jam spikes may start separately. This permits useful source work without claiming that hosting or self-hosted review is ready.

| Stage | Concrete result | Capability needed |
|---|---|---|
| First own-act-model source task | A small Jam declaration and named invariants connecting the existing phrase/rhythm contribution to its intended recorded cue, bar-boundary effect and refusal behavior. Separate symbolic scheduling from authoritative admission. | The supported declaration contract and an explicit dependency/version plan. Do not add a source-tree import to obtain validation. |
| Native application integration | Establish the actual Jam declaration, obtain real member/agent grants, record a contribution and follow its outcome. | A published, runnable establishment/admission/client path for that declaration and exact provenance. Existing `open-pr` creation is repository-specific; assess its fields and grants rather than assuming a generic Jam factory. |
| Hosted musical acceptance | The person and agents contribute through the real room; the intended audible behavior is observed with truthful statuses and recovery. | Deployment, agent/audio ownership, scheduling and listening evidence. Symbolic checks alone cannot satisfy it. |
| Self-hosting the development work | Track, steer and review real Jam development through Artroom. | The real coding workspace, durable conversation/lane custody and review/publication workflow. It is distinct from hosting the musical application. |

Recommended first task: bind the existing contribution/scheduling model to a bounded Jam declaration and its useful invariants, while naming the exact public package and native establishment dependency. Keep the human-hum/agent-response story, timing, retained evidence and actual listening acceptance intact. This recommendation does not replace them with a smaller symbolic demo.

The builder should now state whether that first task can start, and either proceed with its tracked source work or name the one actual missing capability and its owner/release condition. Whole M1/Counting, UX or backlog completion is not an implicit prerequisite. Vocabulary may evolve with bound meanings and retained replay history, as Hugh directed.

One concrete declaration boundary needs a choice in that first task: current Jam note starts/durations and swing can be fractional numbers (`0.35`, `0.5`, `0.7`). Artroom's canonical value format accepts safe integers and refuses fractional numbers. A raw existing Note object therefore cannot simply become a canonical act field unchanged. Choose a versioned, bounded integer time/tempo/swing representation with explicit units and conversion/refusal policy, or an explicitly retained byte/text representation with its own validation. Do not silently round the music or weaken the platform's canonical-number invariant. Local audio calculations may remain floating point; the accepted contribution and its decoder must have a deterministic contract. Reuse existing symbolic notes for the meaningful codec witness rather than starting a new audio benchmark.

Sources inspected: current Jam README, package, AGENTS, original-demo source note and record/phrase timing spans; current Artroom main `18a1288d` directory creation/definition-admission and canonical-number spans; the dated Jam design note header. This is a bounded source assessment, not a full platform or Jam review.
